contentText:
Jelly Roll &#8216;s 18-year-old daughter, Bailee Ann, has hinted that there&#8217;s more to the story of her dad&#8217;s divorce from Bunnie Xo than the public realizes.

Related

Jelly Roll&#8217;s Daughter Bailee Says She&#8217;s &#8216;Disgusted&#8217; by Public Interest in His Divorce From Bunnie&nbsp;Xo

Bunnie Xo Tells Her Side of Jelly Roll Divorce & Says They&#8217;re Still Having a Baby: &#8216;We Are Having Our Little Nugget&nbsp;Together&#8217;

A Timeline of Jelly Roll & Bunnie Xo&#8217;s&nbsp;Relationship

In a TikTok livestream Sunday (July 19), the teenager dismissed commenters asking about her father and stepmother&#8217;s split while also implying that there&#8217;s some shocking information people don&#8217;t know about it &#8212; yet. “Nobody cheated,” she said, according to People . “Period. [Get] the f&#8211;k out of my comments, my DMs, my live with that s&#8211;t. I don’t care. I don’t want to talk about it.&#8221;

Bailee went on to say, “Y’all have no f&#8211;king idea what happened, and wait ‘til y’all find out &#8230; the internet in totality is about to f&#8211;king crumble the day that I open my mouth.&#8221;

&#8220;It’s not a difference in f&#8211;king opinions,” she added, noting that the public does not have a full view of her parents&#8217; relationship, much less how it ended. “Nobody else lived in it. So don’t f&#8211;king even. I’m for real so done. Good? Everybody good? We’re on the same page? Cool.&#8221;

Billboard has reached out to reps for Jelly Roll and Bunnie Xo for comment.

Jelly filed to end his marriage of nearly 10 years in May, news that went public in June. People reported recently that he and Bunnie finalized their divorce in July.

On a since-deleted episode of her Dumb Blonde podcast, Bunnie &#8212; who shares full custody of Bailee with Jelly &#8212; explained that the breakup had been the country star&#8217;s decision, but that she had come to accept it and still considers him one of her best friends. They&#8217;re also planning to move forward with their IVF treatments in the hopes of welcoming a baby together, despite no longer being a couple.

&#8220;We’re going to co-parent together,&#8221; she said at the time. &#8220;We’re going to raise our little nugget as one big, happy family.&#8221;

Both Bunnie and Jelly have also emphasized that infidelity was not a factor in their divorce, with the musician saying on stage at a show in June, “Nobody cheated on nobody &#8230; That will be my best friend forever … Bunnie, I love you, baby. Thank you for those 10 years.&#8221;

But while the former couple has presented a calm, united front in regards to their split, Bailee has expressed frustration about the public&#8217;s interest in it. “I am disgusted at how invested everyone is in a very clearly private family matter,” she wrote on social media in June. “Worry bout your house- not mine. I’m not speaking on it – yet.”

Jelly is currently on tour, alternating between Big Ass Stadium Tour Part 2 coheadlining dates with Post Malone and solo Little Ass Shed Tour shows. He last dropped an album in 2024, reaching No. 1 on the Billboard 200 with Beautifully Broken . He&#8217;s scored 21 Billboard Hot 100 entries to date.
